001100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
001200 PROGRAM-ID.          THDPRT.
001300 AUTHOR.              C HILLES.
001400 DATE-WRITTEN.        12/26/84.
001500 DATE-COMPILED.
001600*INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
001700*
001800*REMARKS.  PRINT HEADER PAGE SUBPROGRAM.
001900*
002000* *** THIS SUBPROGRAM IS CONTAINED IN THE CME ACCOUNT RL ***
002100*
002200*    THIS PROGRAM CAN BE CALLED TO FROM ANY REPORT PROGRAM
002300*    TO PRINT THE HEADER PAGE FOR THE REPORT.  CSIS STANDARDS
002400*    CALL FOR EVERY REPORT PROGRAM HAVING A HEADER PAGE, WHICH
002500*    CONTAINS AN EXPLANATION OF THE REPORT.  MANY PROGRAMS HAVE
002600*    NOT BEEN CONVERTED TO THIS STANDARD (12/28/84).  THIS SUB-
002700*    PROGRAM WILL MAKE IT MUCH EASIER TO ADD A HEADER PAGE TO
002800*    ANY REPORT, BY DOING THE FOLLOWING THINGS:
002900*
003000*      1.  CREATE A FILE CONTAINING THE DATA TO GO ON THE
003100*      HEADER PAGE.  CREATE THE FILE USING EDITOR.  BEFORE
003200*      TYPING IN THE INFO, DO A "/SET LENGTH=80" AND
003300*      "/SET RIGHT=80".  THEN DO AN "AQ" (ADD IN QUIET MODE -
003400*      LINE NUMBERS ARE NOT DISPLAYED).  THIS MAKES IT EASY
003500*      TO DESIGN AN ATTRACTIVE HEADER IN AN 80-COLUMN AREA.
003600*
003700*      2.  SAVE THIS FILE IN THE "PUB" GROUP, UNDER A NAME
003800*      FOLLOWING CSIS CONVENTIONS FOR MPE DATA FILES.
003900*
004000*      3.  IMMEDIATELY AFTER THE OPEN OF YOUR PRINT FILE,
004100*      ADD A CALL TO "GETFNUM" TO OBTAIN THE FILE NUMBER OF
004200*      THE PRINT FILE.
004300*
004400*      4.  AFTER THE CALL TO "GETFNUM" SIMPLY CALL THIS
004500*      PROGRAM ("THDPRT"), PASSING THE NAME OF THE HEADER
004600*      FILE, AND ROUTE DATA (WHO THE REPORT GOES TO - DETERMINED
004700*      BY THE OPTION PROGRAM).  THE HEADER PAGE WIL BE
004800*      PRINTED BEFORE THE ACTUAL REPORT, WITH ROUTING DATA.
004900*
005000*    PARAMETERS
005100*    ----------
005200*
005300* RET-CODE        S9(4) COMP.  A NON-ZERO VALUE WILL BE RETURNED
005400*                 IF A FATAL ERROR OCCURS.
005500*
005600* FILE-NAME       X(17).  PASS THE NAME OF THE HEADER FILE.
005700*
005800* FNUM            S9(4) COMP.  PASS THE MPE FILE NUMBER OF THE
005900*                 PRINT FILE.  THIS CAN BE DETERMINED BY CALLING
006000*                 THE SPL PROGRAM "GETFNUM".
006100*
006200* ROUTE-DATA      X(80).  PASS ROUTING INFORMATION, WHICH MUST BE
006300*                 DETERMINED BY THE OPTION PROGRAM, IN THE
006400*                 FOLLOWING FORMAT:
006500*                   ROUTE-NAME   X(15)   NAME OF PERSON WANTING RPT
006600*                   ROUTE-DEPT   X(4)    THAT PERSON'S DEPT
006700*                   ROUTE-LP     X(3)    LDEV # OF PRINTER
006800*                   ROUTE-USER   X(8)    USERNAME OF ORIGINATOR
006900*                   ROUTE-ACCOUNT X(8)   ACCOUNT NAME OF ORIGINATOR
007000*                   ROUTE-GROUP  X(8)    GROUPNAME OF ORIGINATOR
007100*                   ROUTE-TERM   X(4)    TERMINAL # OF ORIGINATOR
007200*                   FILLER       X(30)
007300*
007400*                 NOTE:  THE ROUTE DATA CAN ONLY BE DETERMINED BY
007500*                 AN OPTION PROGRAM (SUCH AS "TRSCREEN" - WHICH
007600*                 WILL WORK FOR VIRTUALLY ANY REPORT).  IF NO
007700*                 ROUTE DATA IS AVAILABLE, PASS SPACES.
007800*
007900*    12/30/85.
008000*        CHANGED PROGRAM SO THAT IT CAN BE USED TO PRINT A FILE
008100*        ANYWHERE IN A REPORT - WITHOUT THE ROUTING DATA BEING
008200*        PRINTED.  IT WILL DO SO IF CALLED WITH A RETURN CODE
008300*        OF 2.  NOTE THAT THE 0 IS RETURNED IF SUCCESSFUL, THEREFOR
008400*        A 2 WILL HAVE TO BE MOVED IN EACH TIME IT IS CALLED IF
008500*        THE CALLING PROGRAM USES THIS FEATURE.  CIH.
008600*
008700 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
008800 CONFIGURATION SECTION.
008900 SOURCE-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
009000 OBJECT-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
009100 SPECIAL-NAMES. C01 IS NEW-PAGE.
009300
009400 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
009500 FILE-CONTROL.
009600     SELECT HEADER-FILE ASSIGN TO DATABASE-DHDFILE.
           SELECT PRT-FILE ASSIGN TO PRINTER-MCPRT.
009700
009800 DATA DIVISION.
009900 FILE SECTION.
010000 FD  HEADER-FILE
010100     RECORD CONTAINS 92 CHARACTERS.
010200 01  HEADER-REC.
           05  FILLER                 PIC X(12).
           05  HEADER-AREA            PIC X(80).
010300
       FD  PRT-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
           RECORD CONTAINS 132 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS PRT-REC.
       01  PRT-REC                    PIC X(132).

010400 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
010500
010600 77  SAVE-RET-CODE                 PIC S9(4) COMP-4 VALUE 0.
010700
       01  FILE-NAME2                    PIC X(17) VALUE SPACES.
010800*---------- COMPRESSED PRINT ESCAPE SEQUENCE
010900*01  COMPRESS-ESC-SEQ.
011000*    05  FILLER                    PIC X(1)  VALUE %33.
011100*    05  FILLER                    PIC X(4)  VALUE "&k2S".
011200*
011300*---------- STANDARD PRINT PITCH ESCAPE SEQUENCE
011400*01  STANDARD-ESC-SEQ.
011500*    05  FILLER                    PIC X(1)  VALUE %33.
011600*    05  FILLER                    PIC X(4)  VALUE "&k0S".
011700*
       01  IBM-DRAFT-CPI-10    PIC 9(6) BINARY VALUE 196882.
       01  CHAR-10PI-WORK REDEFINES IBM-DRAFT-CPI-10.
           05  FILLER          PIC X(1).
           05  STANDARD-ESC-SEQ PIC X(3).

       01  IBM-DRAFT-CPI-17    PIC 9(6) BINARY VALUE 196879.
       01  CHAR-1636PI-WORK REDEFINES IBM-DRAFT-CPI-17.
           05  FILLER          PIC X(1).
           05  COMPRESS-ESC-SEQ PIC X(3).

011800*************************************************************
011900**                                                          **
